{
  "abstract": "For every n ≥ 47, the least edge count that forces a triangle in an n-vertex simple graph with chromatic number at least five is floor((n−6)²/4) + 6. The proof extends Kenta Kitamura’s result from order 80 down to order 47. It constructs a graph with one fewer edge and bounds the edge count of every triangle-free graph in the stated class.",
